---
import DesignPage from '../../components/DesignPage.astro';
import { elementIndex, elementMeta } from 'parche:registry/elements';
import { ramps, colorRoles, typography, radii, shadows, themes, shadcnAliases, usage } from '../../lib/tokens';

const used = usage(elementMeta as any);
const roleCount = colorRoles.length;
const unused = colorRoles.filter((r) => !(used[`color-${r.short}`]?.length)).map((r) => r.short);
---

<DesignPage title="Design system" description="The design system is the set of --ds- tokens: colour roles, type styles and font roles, each with a light and a dark value. Every element and widget is styled from them and nothing else; a theme is a file that overrides them.">
  <section class="docs-ui mb-12" aria-labelledby="system">
    <h2 id="system" class="type-h2 mb-4">The tokens: <code>--ds-*</code></h2>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Colour roles</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading"><code>--ds-color-&lt;role&gt;</code></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{roleCount} roles — canvas, text, surfaces, primary, status, focus, overlay — each with a light and a dark value. Bridged to Tailwind as <code>bg-surface</code>, <code>text-muted</code>, <code>outline-ring</code>. <a href="/design/colors" class="text-primary underline">Colors</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Type styles</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading"><code>--ds-size-h1</code>, <code>--ds-weight-h1</code>…</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Six styles of four tokens each — size, weight, tracking, leading — composed into <code>.type-h1</code>… <code>.type-label</code>. <a href="/design/typography" class="text-primary underline">Typography</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Font roles</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading"><code>--ds-font-heading</code>, <code>--ds-font-body</code></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Two roles a theme fills with a typeface. Core ships none; the fallback costs no download.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted">Declared in <code>packages/core/src/styles/semantic.css</code>; overridden by a theme under <code>:root[data-theme="…"]</code> and by <code>.dark</code> for the colour mode.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-ui mb-12" aria-labelledby="around">
    <h2 id="around" class="type-h2 mb-4">Beneath it and beside it, not part of it</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Beneath · primitives</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading"><code>--color-&lt;family&gt;-&lt;step&gt;</code></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{ramps.length} OKLCH ramps of 11 steps that the roles point into. Raw material, not tokens of the system: nothing in an element or widget names one directly, and the contract test refuses <code>bg-green-500</code>. A theme may replace a ramp.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted"><code>tokens.css</code></p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Beneath · Tailwind's scale</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading"><code>--radius-*</code>, <code>--shadow-*</code></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{radii.length} radii and {shadows.length} shadows in Tailwind's theme, reached as <code>rounded-md</code> and <code>shadow-lg</code>. There is no <code>--ds-</code> token for shape today; Corporate and Minimal flatten these with a rule instead. <a href="/design/shape" class="text-primary underline">Shape</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted"><code>tokens.css</code></p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border p-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Beside · compatibility</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-semibold text-heading">shadcn/ui names</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{shadcnAliases.length} aliases (<code>--background</code>, <code>--primary</code>…) that point at the roles, so a shadcn component drops in later without a second palette. Applied on top, never used by our elements. <a href="/design/themes#shadcn" class="text-primary underline">The table</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted"><code>shadcn-compat.css</code></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-ui mb-12" aria-labelledby="numbers">
    <h2 id="numbers" class="type-h2 mb-4">At a glance</h2>
    <dl class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <div><dt class="text-muted">Colour roles</dt><dd class="type-h3">{roleCount}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-muted">Consumed by elements</dt><dd class="type-h3">{roleCount - unused.length}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-muted">Type styles</dt><dd class="type-h3">{typography.length}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-muted">Elements on them</dt><dd class="type-h3">{elementIndex.length}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    {unused.length > 0 && (
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Roles no element declares in its <code>tokens</code>: {unused.map((u, i) => <><code>{u}</code>{i < unused.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</>)}. They may still be used by widgets or core; worth a look.</p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="docs-ui mb-12" aria-labelledby="rules">
    <h2 id="rules" class="type-h2 mb-4">The rules</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
      <li><strong class="text-heading">Tokens only.</strong> Elements and widgets use role utilities (<code>bg-surface</code>, <code>text-heading</code>, <code>border-border</code>), never a palette step. That is what lets a theme reskin everything from one file.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-heading">Every role has a light and a dark value</strong>, and the pairs the elements put together must read at WCAG AA. The <a href="/design/colors" class="text-primary underline">Colors</a> page measures them live for the theme and mode you pick above.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-heading">A theme overrides, it does not add.</strong> A theme file may set any primitive or role, and typography, under its own attribute; it may not invent a token the elements do not know.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-heading">Composed type styles</strong> (<code>.type-h1</code>… <code>.type-label</code>) are the only classes core adds; everything else is Tailwind on the bridged roles.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-heading">Only <code>--ds-</code> is the system.</strong> Ramps and Tailwind's scale sit beneath it; the shadcn names sit beside it as a compatibility layer to apply later. Neither is what an element or a theme should reach for first.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

</DesignPage>
